DOMAIN_HINTS:
1. snowflake-ml-python version constraints vary per feature (experiments>=1.19, REST>=1.25)
2. Model version implementations are immutable once logged — only aliases/comments changeable
3. Aliases are the promotion primitive — COPY MODEL does not exist; use ALTER MODEL VERSION SET ALIAS
4. MODEL MONITOR supports binary classification + regression ONLY (not multi-class, despite multi-class perf metrics existing in the function)
5. ExperimentTracking is NOT MLflow — Snowflake-native singleton, not thread-safe, one active run at a time
6. session.call() incompatible with Cortex ML functions — always use session.sql()
7. FeatureView pipeline is immutable after register_feature_view() — only refresh_freq/warehouse/desc updatable
8. Entity join_keys are immutable after creation
9. Model monitor baseline is a snapshot embedded at creation — not a live reference
10. create_service() IS the REST endpoint deployment — same call, ingress_enabled=True

